# The parity corpus is compared byte for byte, so git must not rewrite any of
# it on checkout. On Windows, `core.autocrlf=true` is the default from Git for
# Windows' installer, and it would convert every LF in these files to CRLF --
# after which the binary (Rust's `writeln!` emits LF on every platform) differs
# from its own reference on every single line, for a reason that has nothing to
# do with the port. `-text` disables that conversion in both directions.
#
# parity/check_release.py detects the symptom and says so, but not converting
# is better than diagnosing afterwards.
parity/references/**   -text
parity/fixtures/**     -text
parity/golden_config.ini -text

# Truncated FITS and XISF frames: real binary content, never line-ending
# material, and not worth attempting to diff as text.
parity/fixtures/binary/**  binary
